If `true`, the update or full of this resource takes the snapshot it sends
just before its own transfer, rather than take it with the snapshots of the
other sync resources of the action, at one moment before the first
transfer. Its copy is then of another point in time than theirs, and taken
with no quiesce.

Set it for a dataset whose data is independent of the others, or has to be
sent as late as possible, as the archived logs of a database, which are
complete only once the datafiles are copied.
